The (NH4)2SO4 preparation was fractionated by DEAE Sepharose CL–6B (Fig. 3
                        ). One area of activity against Impranil was detected which was poorly resolved. Samples were collected and pooled (fractions 2–5), and concentrated by ultrafiltration (10,000 Mr cutoff). SDS–PAGE indicated several protein bands as revealed by Coomassie blue staining. Further purification was achieved by Sephadex G75–120 chromatography (Fig. 4
                        ). A single Impranil activity peak was detected in Peak II (fractions 5–10). These fractions were pooled and concentrated by ultrafiltration (10,000 Mr cutoff) for final purification.

The molecular weight of the purified protein was estimated to be 1.15×10−5±0.007 Da by a Dawn DSP–F Laser Photometer using a Zimm Plot method of determination (Fig. 6
                        ). ND–PAGE (Fig. 7
                        A) revealed a single band when visualized by Coomassie blue staining, Rf 0.12. This single protein band co-migrated with Impranilase activity revealed by an Impranilase zymogram (data not shown). SDS–PAGE (Fig. 7B) revealed one major band when visualized by Coomassie blue staining. The polypeptide detected by SDS–PAGE was estimated to have an Mr 29,000 Da, while the ND–PAGE estimated an Mr 116,000 Da.
